  "reason": "Evidence: config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) is the best result at 0.619 acc, and RNA is the dominant signal (rna_only 0.485 vs image_only 0.208). However, we have only tested one RNA encoder (PCA, a linear method), leaving high uncertainty about whether a learned nonlinear representation would improve the RNA branch. Question: Does scvi_n200 (a learned variational representation) outperform PCA in the best-performing architecture? This is a single-variable change from config_018, isolating the RNA encoder effect. Why this is the best next experiment: The RNA encoder is the highest-impact remaining design axis because RNA drives most of the signal. Resolving whether a learned encoder beats PCA either unlocks a major performance gain or eliminates an entire branch of the search space, making it more informative than testing fusion (a likely smaller effect) or image encoder (image signal is weak). It directly extends our strongest evidence with a minimal, interpretable change."
